<section>
  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p>
    A particle is projected from ground level with speed 20 m/s at 45° to
    the horizontal. Take <i>g</i> = 9.81 m/s². Find the time of flight, the
    range, and the greatest height.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><i>u</i> cos 45° = <i>u</i> sin 45° = 14.14 m/s</li>
    <li>Time of flight <i>T</i> = 2 × 14.14 / 9.81 = 2.88 s</li>
    <li>Range <i>R</i> = 14.14 × 2.88 = 40.77 m</li>
    <li>Greatest height <i>H</i> = 14.14² / (2 × 9.81) = 10.19 m</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The same particle is projected from ground level at 30° to the
    horizontal, still at 20 m/s. Find <i>T</i>, <i>R</i>, and <i>H</i>.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><i>u</i> cos 30° = 17.32 m/s, <i>u</i> sin 30° = 10 m/s</li>
    <li><i>T</i> = 2 × 10 / 9.81 = 2.04 s</li>
    <li><i>R</i> = 17.32 × 2.04 = 35.31 m, and <i>H</i> = 100 / 19.62 = 5.10 m</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    On level ground the range is greatest at 45°. From a height, both
    <i>T</i> and <i>R</i> increase.
  </p>
</section>
